### Order Management Test

### Create new order
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "user-123",
  "restaurantId": "restaurant-123",
  "restaurantName": "Pizza Palace",
  "items": [
    {
      "foodId": "food-123",
      "name": "Margherita Pizza",
      "price": 15.99,
      "quantity": 2,
      "specialInstructions": "Extra cheese"
    },
    {
      "foodId": "food-456",
      "name": "Caesar Salad",
      "price": 8.99,
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ],
  "subtotal": 40.97,
  "deliveryFee": 3.99,
  "tax": 3.28,
  "total": 48.24,
  "deliveryAddress": "123 Main St, New York, NY 10001",
  "paymentMethodId": "card-123",
  "notes": "Ring doorbell twice"
}

### Get user orders
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders/user/user-123?limit=10&offset=0

### Get order by ID (replace with actual order ID from creation response)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders/ORDER_ID_HERE

### Update order status
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders/ORDER_ID_HERE/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "confirmed",
  "deliveryPersonName": "John Driver",
  "deliveryPersonPhone": "+1234567890"
}

### Track order
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders/ORDER_ID_HERE/track

### Cancel order
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders/ORDER_ID_HERE

### Test Error Cases

### Create order without required fields
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "restaurantId": "",
  "items": []
}

### Create order with invalid user ID
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "",
  "restaurantId": "restaurant-123",
  "restaurantName": "Pizza Palace",
  "items": [
    {
      "foodId": "food-123",
      "name": "Margherita Pizza",
      "price": 15.99,
      "quantity": 2
    }
  ],
  "subtotal": 31.98,
  "deliveryFee": 3.99,
  "tax": 2.88,
  "total": 38.85,
  "deliveryAddress": "123 Main St, New York, NY 10001",
  "paymentMethodId": "card-123"
}